== Effects ==
* Double tapping a fire key creates a Divine Shield that slowly moves in the chosen direction.
* The Divine Shield has a variety of effects.
** Enemies are pushed back in the opposite direction, completely reversing their trajectory with some added momentum.
*** Enemies pushed into walls or [[obstacles]] take <code>10 + 2 * (floor - 1)</code> damage and deal that same damage to other enemies they collide with.
** Enemy tears are reflected, dealing damage back to enemies depending on the source of the tear.
*** The reflected projectiles deal 6 damage if they would've hurt Isaac for half a heart, and 7 for a full heart.
*** Reflected projectiles do not gain [[Tear effects]] from Isaac.
**** Explosive projectiles (e.g. from {{E|Gurgle}}) explode as normal, dealing as much damage as they would have.
**** Projectiles that create other projectiles (e.g. {{E|Shady}}) can harm Isaac and be reflected.
**** Homing projectiles (e.g. from {{E|Psychic Horf}}) do not retain their homing effect after being reflected.
*** Can reflect:
**** Fire projectiles (e.g. from {{E|Mega Satan}}).
**** Obstacles thrown by {{E|Polty}} or {{E|Kineti}}, dealing a flat 35 damage.
*** Does not reflect:
**** Lines of fire (e.g. from {{E|Dragon Fly}}), but can reflect fireballs (e.g. from {{E|Crackle}}) and their lines of fire do not harm Isaac.
**** Projectiles from {{E|Big Bony}}, {{E|Coal Boy}}, {{E|Danny}}.
** Enemy {{i|Brimstone}} lasers are reflected, dealing 7 damage per tick (105 damage per second) to enemies hit by the reflection. It can even deflect the colossal brimstone laser fired by {{E|The Beast}}.
*** White beams, such as those used by {{E|Dogma}} in its second phase, are reflected into {{I|Revelation}} beams.
* The shield lasts 1 second and has a cooldown of 3 seconds.
* {{transformation contribution|Seraphim}}

== Notes ==
* If any charged item is obtained along with Divine Intervention e.g. {{I|Brimstone}} or Revelation, a different fire key may be pressed to put out the shield without forfeiting the charge of said item.
* The Blindfolded status from certain challenges disables the ability to fire, which also disables the ability to double tap to fire Divine Shields.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Divine Intervention}}: Multiple copies of this item (from effects such as {{I|Diplopia}} or {{I|Crooked Penny}}) have no effect aside from being counted for {{tf|Seraphim}}.

